[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ## Part 1: Design Document Analysis
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ### 1.1 PDF: "Building a Post-Android Phone OS on Existing Android Hardware" (May 2026)
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr **Key findings and their impact on Nuxel:**
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Finding | Impact on Nuxel |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr |---|---|
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Android is not "dying" Sep 2026 — AOSP changes are slower cadence, not death | No panic-driven urgency; project timeline can be realistic |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Five base paths analyzed: Droidian, postmarketOS, Ubuntu Touch, Sailfish, Mobian | Nuxel correctly chose postmarketOS-style mainline-first as its long-term pole |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Banking/ID apps: AOSP-compatible OS is the only reliable path | Nuxel's "no banking promise" non-goal is correctly scoped |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Best strategy: hybrid — Halium bring-up first, then mainline | Nuxel's pure-mainline stance may need a pragmatic Halium bootstrap phase for mustang |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Hardware: pick one friendly family | Nuxel correctly selected Pixel 10 Pro XL as single target |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Qualcomm SoCs and Sony Xperia are best for mainline | Mustang (Tensor G5) is NOT Qualcomm — this is a risk factor |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Hybrid approach: vendor kernel reuse → Linux userspace → mainlining | Nuxel may need to accept a vendor-kernel bootstrap phase for mustang |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr **Critical misalignment:** The PDF strongly advocates a **hybrid staged approach** (Halium/vendor kernel first, then mainline). Nuxel's design explicitly forbids Halium, libhybris, and vendor kernel reuse. For mustang, where mainline support is extremely preliminary (UART/initramfs only as of Nov 2025), this pure-mainline stance may be a **blocker** for the first 12-18 months.
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr **Recommendation:** Add a "Phase 0" that uses the Google `android-gs-mustang-6.12` vendor kernel as a bring-up kernel, with explicit plan to replace with mainline LTS once device-tree patches are upstreamed. This is the pragmatic path the PDF recommends.
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
