[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr # Nuxel OS: Init System & Service Management
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr > **Status:** Definitive — documents the two independent init systems used
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr > across the two Nuxel deployment targets.
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr >
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr > **Target device:** Google Pixel 10 Pro XL (mustang) — serial: 58211FDCQ001LA
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr > **VM platform:** UTM on Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3/M4)
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ---
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ## 1. Decision (D.3): Two init systems, never mixed
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr Nuxel deliberately targets **two different init systems** for its two
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr deployment targets. This is a documented design decision (D.3) — each target's
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr init files are **self-consistent** and must **not** be mixed or cross-installed.
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Target | Distro / platform | Init system |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr |--------|-------------------|-------------|
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | **(A) Fedora VM** | Fedora-ARM64 under UTM on Apple Silicon | **systemd** |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | **(B) Alpine / pmOS mustang** | Alpine Linux / postmarketOS on the Pixel 10 Pro XL | **OpenRC** |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr These two paths live in separate directories and are consumed by the build
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr scripts for the respective targets. Keeping them isolated is what lets a single
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr repo serve both the VM development loop and the physical-device boot.
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr > **Rule:** Do NOT install a systemd unit into the Alpine/pmOS mustang image and
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr > do NOT install an OpenRC script into the Fedora-ARM64 VM image.
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ---
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ## 2. (A) systemd — Fedora-ARM64 VM target
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr The Fedora VM image is bootstrapped by `images/mkrootfs.sh` and uses **systemd**
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr for both system-level daemons and per-user session units. The systemd-managed
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr service set is:
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-bridge`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-http-bridge`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-notifications`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-portal`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-home-native`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-home-kiosk`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr - `nuxel-phosh-agent`
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr ### 2.1 System-level units (`services/*/systemd/*.service`)
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr 
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | Unit file | One-line purpose |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr |-----------|------------------|
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | `services/nuxel-bridge/systemd/nuxel-bridge.service` | Nuxel Bridge — D-Bus mediator between PWAs and native phone functions (system bus). |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | `services/nuxel-bridge/systemd/nuxel-http-bridge.service` | Nuxel HTTP Bridge API — exposes a localhost HTTP API for the PWA layer. |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | `services/nuxel-notifications/systemd/nuxel-notifications.service` | Nuxel Notification Hub — D-Bus notification daemon with persistence. |
[0m[36m[Qlarifier] stderr | `services/nuxel-portal/systemd/nuxel-portal.service` | Nuxel Portal Daemon — user-consent GTK4 permission gateway (system bus, root). |
