[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr ===kernel patch head===
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr From: Nuxel Project <nuxel@nuxel.org>
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr Subject: [PATCH] Nuxel phone features for Google Pixel 10 Pro XL (mustang)
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr Add support for the Nuxel phone OS on the Google Pixel 10 Pro XL (mustang,
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr Tensor G5 / gs501).
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr The Nuxel additions are kept in a self-contained subsystem under
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr drivers/soc/google/ so that `make olddefconfig` recognizes and retains the
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr CONFIG_NUXEL* symbols instead of silently stripping them from a config that
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr declares them.  A minimal source stub is provided so the Makefile targets
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr exist at build time.
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr Changes:
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr - gs501_defconfig: declare CONFIG_NUXEL / CONFIG_NUXEL_PHONE /
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   CONFIG_NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM.
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr - drivers/soc/google/Kconfig: add CONFIG_NUXEL, CONFIG_NUXEL_PHONE and
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   CONFIG_NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM with help text and proper dependencies.
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr - drivers/soc/google/Makefile + drivers/soc/google/nuxel-phone.c: add a
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   compile-time Nuxel SoC object (empty stub that builds to a valid .o).
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr - Only genuine, upstream-verifiable kernel symbols are referenced; all
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   previously-added aspirational symbols (DRM_POWERVR_DXT,
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   TOUCHSCREEN_SAMSUNG_S6SY791, MHI_SAMSUNG_EXYNOS5500, MHI_SAMSUNG,
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   MHI_BUS_PCI_GENERIC_GS, DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_AMB655X, NFC_NXP_SN220,
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr   INPUT_GOODIX_GF3636, INPUT_GOODIX_GFX, BRCMFMAC_BCM4390, BT_HCIBCM4390,
