[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //                                   `org.nuxel.Home` by default, mirroring how
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //                                   nuxel-home uses a module-level `bridge`.
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr // CONTRACT (shared across all PWAs)
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //   ─────────────────────────────────
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //   * Token handling: unlike the old home bridge (which hardcoded a static
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //     dev token), this module fetches the current API token from the server
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //     via `GET /api/v1/token`, caches it in `localStorage` under the key
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //     `nuxel-bridge-token`, and transparently refreshes it whenever an API
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //     call is rejected with HTTP 401.  No static/temporary token is ever
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //     embedded in the client.
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr //
