[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr ## What is Nuxel?
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr Nuxel is a mobile-first Linux OS built from scratch on a pure Linux substrate. It borrows the **security mindset** of GrapheneOS without borrowing Android as the base platform.
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | | Nuxel | Android | GrapheneOS |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr |---|---|---|---|
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | Base | Linux 6.12 LTS | AOSP/Linux | AOSP/Linux |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | Shell | Phosh + GTK4 | SurfaceFlinger | SurfaceFlinger |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | Apps | PWA + native C | APK | APK |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | Sandbox | 5-layer (ns+seccomp+Landlock+AppArmor+nftables) | SELinux | SELinux + hardened |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | Immutable | dm-verity + AVB | dm-verity + AVB | dm-verity + AVB |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr | Android deps | **ZERO** | Full AOSP | Full AOSP |
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr ## Architecture
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr 
[0m[35m[instruQtor] stderr ```
